    "Most positive records are case reports or disease cohorts rather than controlled induction studies",
    "The negative betamethasone patch test is for a different corticosteroid and does not exclude the query",
    "L2 records are nonvoting context and were not counted as independent gold votes"
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted risk: spironolactone is a lipophilic neutral steroid with direct-acting enone and thioester alerts; multiple transferable human positive outcomes for thioester/enone steroids (tixocortol pivalate, testosterone esters, enoxolone, hydrocortisone aceponate) support sensitization, while the only relevant negative (betamethasone) is less transferable and the L2 context adds a positive corticosteroid ester."
}

